@ 28.2 - Proto-Muskogean to Proto-Western Muskogean
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Booker, Karen (2005), “Muskogean Historical Phonology”. In Hardy, Heather Kay, and Janine Scancarelli, eds., Native Languages of the Southeastern United States 246 – 298
	ts tʃ > s ts
	θ > n
	s > ʃ
	x > h
	C₁:[+weak] C₂:[+weak] > ʔ h / V_V#
	V > ∅ / V{k,ʔ,h}_#
	xʷ > h / %_{o,i}(C)#
	a > o / xʷ_#
	oj aj > i:[+long] {a:[+long],i:[+long]}
	i > ∅ / #(C)V(C)(C)V(C)(C)_# (sporadic in the case of other vowels)
	tl st > l:[+long] t:[+long]